comments.body:
Could be something wrong when deserializing binary string or the query got killed somehow by the server.

> A similar query succeeds if we directly query Clickhouse.

@reporter, did you check table `system.query_log` or error log in ClickHouse? Just trying to understand if there's any clue there and the exact query being sent to ClickHouse.

@participant1, could this relate to push-down support in ClickHouse connector? When using `date(date) in (date'2023-04-06', date'2023-04-09')`, a query like `SELECT "date", "advertisable_eid", "domain" FROM "default"."trino"` will be sent to ClickHouse. If you change the criteria to `date(date) = date'2023-04-06'`, the query will be changed to `SELECT "date", "advertisable_eid", "domain" FROM "default"."trino" WHERE ("date" >= '2023-04-06' AND "date" < '2023-04-07')`.
